{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"","type":"thinking"},{"text":"Build clean. Now add a caller-propagation assertion (eval-path's result depends on the store) after the `mytool` scenario:","type":"text"},{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01Hkr8NUp7tVkhiZB5bXCKPj","input":{"file_path":"tests/secrets/cli.sh","new_string":"echo \"  ok: a reader naming a repo path grants the secret\" >&2\n\necho \"== eval-path folds secret-hash, so a worker's callers become per-user ==\" >&2\n# mytool matches the deploytok reader, so eval-path marks its returned arg tree.\n# With the secret removed it matches nothing, so the result differs — which is\n# exactly what makes anything embedding mytool per-user.\nwithsecret=$(\"$CAOS_CLI\" eval-path mytool) || fail \"eval-path mytool failed\"\nrm .caos-secrets/deploytok\nwithout=$(\"$CAOS_CLI\" eval-path mytool) || fail \"eval-path mytool (no secret) failed\"\n[ \"$withsecret\" != \"$without\" ] \\\n  || fail \"eval-path mytool should depend on the secret store (got '$withsecret' both times)\"\necho \"  ok: mytool's eval result differs with vs without its granted secret\" >&2","old_string":"echo \"  ok: a reader naming a repo path grants the secret\" >&2"},"name":"edit","type":"tool_use"}],"results":[{"content":[{"text":"result tree: bin image std time","type":"text"}],"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CbAKKQLpvFbNN2dji1LaCj","type":"tool_result"}],"v":1}